<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48588" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωρ-ητικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>able to perceive</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ περὶ τὰ σώματα κάλλους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1338b1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ πάντων θ. ἀλλὰ ἐνίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					2.108S.
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς ἀφροσύνης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>M.</u>
					11.256
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of the mind,
				<i>contemplative, speculative</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ
				περὶ τὴν . . οὐσίαν θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1005a35
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ περὶ φύσεως θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>PA</u>
				641a29
			</span></i>: c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαντικὴ ἐπιστήμη θ. τοῦ . . μέλλοντος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Def.</u>
					414b
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστήμη θ., διάνοια</span>,
			opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρακτική, ποιητική</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1064a17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1025b25
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>de An.</u>
					415a11
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. βίος</span>
			<i>a contemplative</i> or <i>speculative</i> life (opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπολαυστικός, πολιτικός</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>EN</u>
				1095b19
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cic.</u>
				3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. φιλόσοφος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Per.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herm.
					<u>in Phdr.</u>
					p.59A.
				</span></i>
			
			Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Nat.</u>
					28.7
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				4.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>Comm.Math.</u>
				20
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωρικός</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cod.Just.</u>
				10.56.1.1
			</span></i>.</div>
